<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="AFRO 132" href="schedule/2021/fall/AFRO/132.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2021" href="schedule/2021.xml">2021</calendarYear><term id="120218" href="schedule/2021/fall.xml">Fall 2021</term><subject id="AFRO" href="schedule/2021/fall/AFRO.xml">African American Studies</subject></parents><label>African American Music</label><description>Survey of African American music, from its origins to the present with a focus on understanding details of musical performance and the ways in which music interacts with its social and political context. Examines genres such as spirituals, the blues, jazz, R&amp;B, soul, and hip-hop. No previous musical background is necessary.</description><creditHours>3 hours.</creditHours><sectionDegreeAttributes>Humanities - Lit &amp; Arts, and Cultural Studies - US Minority course.</sectionDegreeAttributes><genEdCategories><category id="CS"><description>Cultural Studies</description><ns2:genEdAttributes><genEdAttribute code="1US">Cultural Studies - US Minority</genEdAttribute></ns2:genEdAttributes></category><category id="HUM"><description>Humanities &amp; the Arts</description><ns2:genEdAttributes><genEdAttribute code="1LA">Humanities – Lit &amp; Arts</genEdAttribute></ns2:genEdAttributes></category></genEdCategories><sections><section id="75548" href="schedule/2021/fall/AFRO/132/75548.xml">AD1</section><section id="75549" href="schedule/2021/fall/AFRO/132/75549.xml">AD2</section><section id="75550" href="schedule/2021/fall/AFRO/132/75550.xml">AD3</section><section id="75551" href="schedule/2021/fall/AFRO/132/75551.xml">AD4</section><section id="67122" href="schedule/2021/fall/AFRO/132/67122.xml">JM1</section></sections></ns2:course>